                                                "sense_id": "fef49eff-b8e8-30e6-aa62-cb80e4acb832",
                                                "text": "2017, Jennifer S. Holland, For These Monkeys, It’s a Fight for Survival., National Geographic (March 2017)http://www.nationalgeographic.com/magazine/2017/03/macaques-monkeys-indonesia-endangered-pet-trade/\nThe town of Tompasobaru, a six-hour drive from Tangkoko, is known for the fragrant cloves that carpet the front yards of homes, drying on tarps in the sun. But in the town’s open market, the air hung heavy with the metallic smell of the butcher’s wares."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0d0de560-1de4-3a69-98f0-8ba384e41578",
                                        "entry_id": "48b639d6-3467-3380-84b5-c80d9788ace6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To reprimand."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28195b72-374c-432f-b96e-47322a32f9a3",
                                                "sense_id": "0d0de560-1de4-3a69-98f0-8ba384e41578",
                                                "text": "Even Colonel Yakov, so recently carpeted by St Petersburg, was reported to be back in the Pamirs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91596817-cc98-48f6-849d-b6c8f7f5ee98",
                                                "sense_id": "0d0de560-1de4-3a69-98f0-8ba384e41578",
                                                "text": "At 4pm, the phone went. It was The Sun: 'We hear your daughter's been expelled for cheating at her school exams...'\nShe'd made a remark to a friend at the end of the German exam and had been pulled up for talking.\nAs they left the exam room, she muttered that the teacher was a 'twat'. He heard and flipped—a pretty stupid thing to do, knowing the kids were tired and tense after exams. Instead of dropping it, the teacher complained to the Head and Deb was carpeted."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
